/-!
# Packed candidate J₂ coset representatives and edge witnesses

Each proposed representative is encoded by its index in the already-certified
100 × 63 × 24 × 4 normal forms, avoiding repeated reduction of long BFS words.
The index is i0 + 100*(i1 + 63*(i2 + 24*i3)), packed in 20 bits. Each edge
witness is u + 5*v in 5 bits. Blocks contain 128 little-endian entries.
These are candidate data only; no edge or coverage assertion is made here.

Source and attribution: Presentation/source/README.md; original Apache-2.0
transcription script: Geometry/source/generate_schreier_data.py.
-/

